WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.650
We've been following the investigation that
the FBI and local law enforcement and other

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:10.999
agencies have been doing into the riotous
insurrectionists from January 6th and over

00:00:10.999 --> 00:00:14.440
the weekend and over the last couple of days,
more and more people have been getting arrested

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:15.440
and booked.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.130
And we've seen the mug shots and we've seen
all of it.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.500
But one of the questions has been, are they
going to throw the book at these folks?

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.610
What are the charges going to be?

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:24.630
Is jail time prison time likely?

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:29.270
And we got a little bit of insight into that
yesterday at a joint press conference involving

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:34.620
the Justice Department and the FBI, where
the latest data is that one hundred and seventy

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:41.500
cases have been opened and many folks are
going to be facing some pretty serious charges.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:47.260
Of the 170 people found so far, 70 have been
charged.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:50.760
And that's expected to grow into the hundreds.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:57.780
Notably, there are many who will be facing
charges of sedition, which carries up to 20

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.329
years in prison.

00:00:59.329 --> 00:01:02.000
Here is video from the press conference.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Take a listen.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:09.040
We're looking at significant felony cases
tied to sedition and conspiracy.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:14.790
Just yesterday, our office organized a strike
force of very senior national security prosecutors

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:16.810
and public corruption prosecutors.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:21.240
They're only marching orders from are to build.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:25.780
Seditious and conspiracy charges relate to
the most heinous acts that occurred in the

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:30.830
capital, and these are significant charges
that have felonies with prison terms of up

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:32.729
to 20 years.

00:01:32.729 --> 00:01:37.140
In addition to that, we're looking and taking
a priority with cases in which weapons were

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:41.170
involved and cases in which destructive devices
were involved.

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:45.520
As people know, through news reports, there
were pipe bombs found outside the capital.

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:47.030
The ATF is working on that.

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:48.710
Metro police is working on that.

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:54.750
FBI is working on that to find that individual
or individuals who planted those devices.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:02:00.479
So in addition to just those cases we're looking
at, we're going to focus on the most significant

00:02:00.479 --> 00:02:05.729
charges as a deterrent, because regardless
of if it was just a trespass in the capital

00:02:05.729 --> 00:02:10.450
or if someone planted a pipe bomb, you will
be charged and you will be found.

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:12.970
So there's much to discuss here.

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:20.350
First of all, just because they are seeking
certain charges or even filing certain charges

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:26.140
initially tells us very little about how much
prison time, if any, these individuals are

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:27.140
going to do.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:28.600
And we're going to talk through that.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:35.640
Now, in the background of all of this is another
issue, which is that the question of murder

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:41.920
charges also needs to be considered for those
involved in the deaths that took place.

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:45.239
But we'll get to that sort of when when we
come to it.

00:02:45.239 --> 00:02:48.450
I do think it's important that we temper our
expectations.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:50.099
And I'll give you an example of that.

00:02:50.099 --> 00:02:52.130
And I got a few emails from lawyers about
this.

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:57.300
My instinct was this and then a few lawyers
in the audience emailed me about it.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:04.750
Sedition is a very high bar to meet in a court
of law and arguably for good reason, because

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:06.510
it's an extremely serious charge.

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:09.540
It's essentially a crime against your country
in a way.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:15.290
And so I doubt we will see many sedition convictions,
if any.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:20.170
The legal definition of sedition is is precise
and we'll look at it.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:26.760
But my expectation is we're going to see people
go down for lesser charges, likely still federal

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:31.680
charges, many with some prison time associated
as well.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:38.310
But sedition is the act of inciting revolt
or violence against the lawful authority with

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:43.640
the this is the key part with the goal of
destroying or overthrowing it.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:45.580
This is very much like perjury.

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:50.730
And we've talked before about how, colloquially
speaking, perjury takes place all the time

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.730
during trials.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:54.819
People get up there and they say things that
aren't true.

00:03:54.819 --> 00:03:57.599
And and to some degree, they know that they're
not true.

00:03:57.599 --> 00:04:01.989
But proving perjury because you need to prove
intent to deceive is difficult.

00:04:01.989 --> 00:04:04.660
And it doesn't happen very often.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:06.160
Many I don't know about.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:11.290
Most it's very common that in a murder case,
you have witnesses who say opposite things

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:15.270
and to some degree they know that they are
unlikely to be telling what they know to be

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:16.590
the full truth.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:18.289
But you don't see perjury charges.

00:04:18.289 --> 00:04:23.379
You don't, because it's very difficult to
prove and a lot of work for prosecutors much,

00:04:23.379 --> 00:04:28.939
much like with sedition, because the goal
of destroying or overthrowing the authority

00:04:28.939 --> 00:04:31.259
is part of the definition of sedition.

00:04:31.259 --> 00:04:32.430
A good lawyer.

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:35.159
And some of these people are going to have
good lawyers.

00:04:35.159 --> 00:04:36.800
Many will not, but some will.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:43.520
A good lawyer is going to be able to defeat
or at least introduce significant doubt about

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:46.849
the intent of the actions.

00:04:46.849 --> 00:04:53.069
They will say maybe, listen, they're on camera
breaking the window or doing this or doing

00:04:53.069 --> 00:04:57.210
this in Nancy Pelosi's office or whatever
the thing is.

00:04:57.210 --> 00:05:02.000
But disturbing the peace, trespassing, you
know, whatever.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.830
But to show intent to overthrow is going to
be really tough.

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:10.309
Now, some of these people were dumb enough
to post their intentions on social media.

00:05:10.309 --> 00:05:13.460
And in those cases, it will be more difficult
to overcome.

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:19.419
But the point is, you know, life is weird
in that way and there are good reasons for

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:21.649
it in many cases.

00:05:21.649 --> 00:05:27.339
But I think we should just be be realistic
about what what our expectations should be.

00:05:27.339 --> 00:05:33.330
The other the other thing that sometimes will
happen is that events where things are done

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:41.479
as a group, you might much more easily be
able to say as a group, this was seditious

00:05:41.479 --> 00:05:43.120
as a group.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:47.009
What this was, was the attempted overthrow
of an authority.

00:05:47.009 --> 00:05:51.479
But that doesn't necessarily mean you can
apply that exact same intent, an agency to

00:05:51.479 --> 00:05:53.419
the individual person in a court of law.

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:58.020
And to be clear, I'm talking only what we
are expecting to happen in a court of law.

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:00.990
So the point is, let's wait and see.

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:05.819
But the good news so far is that the number
of people charged is soon to get into the

00:06:05.819 --> 00:06:08.840
hundred over one hundred, and it really should
go significantly higher.

